{# ============================================================
   THE PAGE'S RUNTIME STRINGS

   Everything app.js says while a round is being played, as inert
   JSON for www/shared/i18n.js to read. Two sources, merged here:
   src/content/<lang>/shared.json (chat, the cross-game room lookup)
   and this page's own `runtime` block.

   data-lang is the tag the Intl formatters use, and is NOT always the
   html lang. The site's English copy is British, and en-US would give
   Intl.ListFormat an Oxford comma the rest of the copy does not use.

   type="application/json" is not executable, so nothing here runs; the
   browser hands it over as text and i18n.js parses it once.

   data-paths is every language this page exists in, as `lang:url` pairs.
   shared/lang.js reads it to decide where to send a player whose room is in
   another language (#138). It comes from `page.locales` in site.json, the
   same source as the hreflang block, so the client cannot drift from the
   set of pages that were actually built. A page with one language still
   emits it; the map simply has one entry and no redirect can ever fire.
   data-games is every GAME page the build produced, as `game:lang:url`
   triples. data-paths above is this page in other languages; this is every
   other page too, which is what the cross-game room lookup needs: a Spanish
   Draw code typed on the Spanish Word page has to reach /es/draw/ in one hop
   rather than bouncing off /draw/ and an English modal (#159). Same source as
   everything else, so a game that has no page in a language simply has no
   entry and the lookup falls back to the default language rather than
   inventing a path.
   ============================================================ #}
<script type="application/json" id="i18n" data-lang="{{ locale.intl }}" data-paths="{% for a in alternates %}{{ a.lang }}:{{ a.path }}{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}" data-games="{% for g in gameLinks %}{{ g.game }}:{{ g.lang }}:{{ g.path }}{% if not loop.last %} {% endif %}{% endfor %}">{{ i18nBundle | safe }}</script>
